    "narrative": "Our primary focus today is capitalizing on the favorable matchup against Lowder, who sports a 4.72 xERA. **Corbin Carroll** is our clear headliner with an elite 85.94 score; his combination of order placement and a slow opposing delivery maximizes his stolen base equity, a critical component of our strategy given our obsession with speed. **Mickey Moniak** also earns a massive 75.98 rating, as the park factors and platoon advantage against Bibee align perfectly for a high-output performance. We are similarly bullish on **Gabriel Moreno** (70.08) and **Seiya Suzuki** (69.65), both of whom benefit from positive SP skill metrics and prime lineup positioning to drive production.\n\nWhile our roster is optimized, the bench decision regarding **Cole Young** was the most difficult. Despite his 45.54 score, **Cole Young** ultimately lost out because his lower efficiency metrics compared to the rest of the utility core left him as a luxury item rather than a necessity. We also opted to keep **Jose Caballero** benched against the stiff 2.94 xERA of Cease; even with a favorable SB environment, the difficulty of the opposing pitcher makes him a poor start for a day where we must preserve game caps. **James Wood** remains sidelined on the IL, but we are monitoring his progress to bolster our bench depth in the coming weeks. Owners should note that while **Brice Turang** holds a strong 66.34 score, his efficiency is slightly hampered by a platoon disadvantage against P\u00e9rez, though his #2 spot in the order keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start category.",
